   \item Number of carrots left = 12 - 2 = 10 carrots
   \end{itemize}
2. Next, calculate the number of carrots Nancy picked the
next day.
   \begin{itemize}
   \item Nancy picked 21 more carrots.
   \item Number of carrots picked = 21
   \end{itemize}
3. Finally, calculate the total number of carrots Nancy
had.
   \begin{itemize}
   \item Total number of carrots = Number of carrots after
throwing out - Number of carrots picked
   \item Total number of carrots = 10 + 21 = 31
   \end{itemize}
Therefore, Nancy would have 31 carrots total.

\boxed{31}

